{"skill_id":"app-examples","version":1,"questions":[{"id":"app-examples-r1-q1","version":1,"round":1,"type":"mc","prompt":"A mixing tank has inflow rate \\(q_{in}\\) and outflow rate \\(q_{out} = h/R\\), where \\(h\\) is the level and \\(R\\) is the hydraulic resistance. The state is","options":["the level \\(h\\)","the inflow rate","the outflow rate","the resistance \\(R\\)"],"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The level is a stored quantity that needs an initial condition. The inflow is an input, not a state. The outflow is a function of the state, not the state itself. The resistance is a parameter, not a dynamic quantity.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>tank level</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,127.8 52,122.9 55.1,118.4 58.1,114 61.1,109.9 64.1,106.1 67.2,102.4 70.2,99 73.2,95.7 76.2,92.6 79.2,89.7 82.3,86.9 85.3,84.3 88.3,81.8 91.3,79.4 94.4,77.2 97.4,75.1 100.4,73.1 103.4,71.3 106.4,69.5 109.5,67.8 112.5,66.2 115.5,64.7 118.5,63.3 121.6,61.9 124.6,60.7 127.6,59.5 130.6,58.3 133.6,57.2 136.7,56.2 139.7,55.3 142.7,54.3 145.7,53.5 148.8,52.7 151.8,51.9 154.8,51.2 157.8,50.5 160.8,49.8 163.9,49.2 166.9,48.6 169.9,48.1 172.9,47.5 176,47 179,46.6 182,46.1 185,45.7 188,45.3 191.1,44.9 194.1,44.6 197.1,44.3 200.1,43.9 203.2,43.6 206.2,43.4 209.2,43.1 212.2,42.8 215.2,42.6 218.3,42.4 221.3,42.1 224.3,